    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d872">

                <pb facs="1004" n="810" xml:id="pg810"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Frankfurt <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">USPolAd</hi> Files—500 Potsdam
                    Conference</note>
                <head>No. 872<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Proposal by the Soviet
                        Delegation</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d872-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation?]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-23">July 23, 1945</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article</hi> 19 <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">of “Economic Principles”</hi></p>
                <p>19. After payment of Reparations enough resources must be left to enable the
                    German people to subsist without external assistance. In working out the
                    economic balance of Germany the necessary means must be provided for payment for
                    imports approved by the Control Council. In case the means are insufficient to
                    pay simultaneously on reparations account and for approved imports all kinds of
                    deliveries (internal consumption, exports, reparations) have to be
                    proportionally reduced.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d872-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d872-f1-content">
                <p>This is apparently the first Soviet draft on this subject presented at the Sixth
                    Meeting of the Foreign Ministers, July 23. See <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg279">p. 279</ref>. It bears the following manuscript
                    notation by Murphy: “Submitted by
                        Molotov July 23”.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
